def dif_Square(n: int) -> bool:
    """
    Determine if the integer n can be expressed as a difference of two squares:
    n = a^2 - b^2, where a and b are any integers (positive, negative, or zero).

    Since a^2 - b^2 = (a-b)(a+b), n can be represented as such if and only if
    n can be factored into two integers p and q of the same parity (both even or both odd),
    because (a-b) and (a+b) must have the same parity.

    Args:
